    "turn_text": "Amen and you know, there are we we have we did do a veterans bill that was was pretty significant a couple weeks ago, but for the most part you particularly around health care we've We've seen a lot of nothing we've seen a lot of fire and brimstone But no action and in the meantime we're seeing a meltdown of our health care system in Obamacare, and that doesn't need to happen. I mean, the one good thing that perhaps came out of the final effort where the Republicans themselves couldn't muster enough votes to pass health care was there's a whole lot of us in both parties that said, when we get back in September, we actually got to fix this now. Let's get past the, you know, your border against it, repeal, replace. Let's just fix. And there are certain things we can do. I know that would Stop the increase in rates or get some of the insurance companies back in we could frankly just have the law be enforced in terms of the Reimbursements that go into these risk sharing pools the very sick people who drive up the overall cost they would be in a separate pool more handled by the government. I think we are going to have to deal with the question. If you like the part of the bill that says you can't be discriminated against if you have a preexisting condition, the only way you can keep that is by having some level of requirement that if you can afford health insurance, you buy it because if not, people will wait until they get sick.",
