    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. The question is are there also enough? fellow Republicans who are willing to change the discussion that this has to all be done by one team. I mean, one of the valid criticism of Obamacare was it got all passed by Democrats. Then you ended up seeing the repeal effort only done by Republicans. So if we've learned nothing from this, it ought to be neither party's got a monopoly on good or bad ideas. And maybe we ought to try to get rid of the bad and just work on the good ideas together. And I think there's a lot of us in both parties who are pretty darn fed up and also frankly embarrassed by how little the Congress has done the last few months. That may mean that we have to break with the party leaders who want to just make fun of the other side, but the country deserves better.",
